<title>USA: Barney's creditors call Dickson bid low.</title>
<headline>Barney's creditors call Dickson bid low.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Official Committee of Unsecured Creditors of Barney's Inc said on Tuesday the committee has rejected Dickson Concepts (International) Ltd's bid to acquire the bankrupt U.S.-based retailer.</p>
<p>The committee said it believes the value of the company is substantially in excess of Dickson's proposal.  </p>
<p>Dickson has offered Barney's current owners $240 million cash investment and a minority stake in Barney's non-U.S. store licensing income.</p>
<p>Barney's and creditors committee representatives were not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
